 public:
  explicit CustomOpKernel(OpKernelConstruction* ctx) : OpKernel(ctx) {}
  void Compute(OpKernelContext* ctx) override {
    // Implementation placeholder
  }
};

REGISTER_KERNEL_BUILDER(Name("CustomOp").Device(DEVICE_CPU), CustomOpKernel);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor correctness across CPU vs GPU builds?
- How would you handle versioned breaking changes to the op signature?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design low-latency multimodal inference on TF Serving, including shared encoders, caching, and batch policy.

## Key Concepts
- Multimodal architecture; dynamic batching; caching; TF-TRT; canary updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo config sketch
model_config_list {
  config {
    name: 'multimodal'
    dynamic_batching {
      max_batch_size: 64
      batch_queue_capacity: 128
      fbatch_timeout_micros: 50000
      num_batch_threads: 4
      allow_precision_loss: true
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure tail latency and instrument per-queue metrics?
- How would you invalidate cached image embeddings when inputs change?
